PROSPECTIVE COMPONENT REQUIREMENTS (Emergency Module)
======================================================
R1: Emergency Triggering  
While operating in Normal mode, exactly two administrators are required to jointly trigger an emergency, causing the system to enter Emergency mode immediately when both administrators trigger simultaneously.

R2: Emergency Duration  
Emergency mode is active only for a fixed (predetermined) duration, with an option to manually end the Emergency mode early; after which the system must automatically return to Normal mode if not ended manually before.

R3: Emergency Mode Behavior  
During Emergency mode:  
  R3.1: Request processing may bypass the usual FIFO order to prioritize processing multiple requests classified as High simultaneously.  
  R3.2: Users are allowed to temporarily hold mutually exclusive roles, relaxing the exclusivity constraints enforced during Normal mode by completely suspending these constraints.  
  R3.3: Administrators temporarily gain emergency privileges exclusive to Emergency mode.  
  R3.4: Delegated roles can be assigned as usual, respecting existing clearance and delegation constraints.

R4: Post-Emergency Restoration  
After Emergency mode ends:  
  R4.1: All emergency privileges held by administrators must be revoked.  
  R4.2: All roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked. Delegated roles assigned prior to Emergency mode remain active unless expired or revoked by an administrator.  
  R4.3: Administrators must update their credentials immediately after Emergency mode ends and before any further system interaction.

KEY CONCEPTS AND ENTITIES
==========================
- User: An entity representing a system user, assigned a clearance level and roles (assigned or delegated).  
- Administrator: A user subtype with High clearance and additional administrative privileges.  
- Role: A set of permissions assigned to users; roles have clearance requirements and exclusivity constraints defined as static pairs of mutually exclusive roles.  
- Delegated Role: A temporary role assigned from a higher-clearance user to a lower-clearance user, subject to expiration or revocation.  
- Security Clearance Level: An ordered level (High > Medium > Low) assigned to users determining access rights.  
- System Object: An entity affected by actions; each has a classification level (High, Medium, Low).  
- Request: A user-submitted action affecting one or more system objects, classified by the highest classification of those objects.  
- Emergency Mode: A system operational mode triggered by exactly two administrators simultaneously, enabling special behaviors and privileges for a fixed duration or until manually ended early.  
- Emergency Privilege: A temporary privilege granted to administrators during Emergency mode.  
- Role Exclusivity: Constraints preventing users from holding mutually exclusive roles simultaneously (defined as static pairs), which are completely suspended during Emergency mode.  
- FIFO Order: The default ordering of request processing during Normal mode.  
- Mode: The system operational state, either Normal or Emergency.

ASSUMPTIONS REQUIRING CLARIFICATION
====================================
1. The system transitions immediately to Emergency mode as soon as exactly two administrators trigger the emergency simultaneously, with no ordering or delay between triggering actions.  
2. Emergency mode has a fixed, predetermined duration, but also supports manual early termination by authorized administrators.  
3. Mutually exclusive roles are defined as static pairs of roles; during Emergency mode, exclusivity constraints are completely suspended, allowing users to hold mutually exclusive roles simultaneously.  
4. Updating credentials by administrators after Emergency mode is a mandatory action required immediately after Emergency ends and must be completed before any further system interaction.  
5. Delegated roles can continue to be assigned during Emergency mode as usual. Upon exiting Emergency mode, only delegated roles assigned during Emergency mode are automatically revoked; delegated roles assigned prior to Emergency mode remain unless expired or explicitly revoked by an administrator.

CONSTRAINTS
===========
- During Normal mode, request processing strictly follows FIFO order.  
- Users can only submit requests with classification less than or equal to their clearance.  
- Role delegation must respect clearance constraints and is temporary with expiration or revocation possible at any time.  
- Exactly two administrators are required simultaneously to trigger Emergency mode; no fewer or more administrators can trigger it alone.  
