- During Emergency mode, multiple high-classification requests can be processed concurrently, bypassing FIFO order.  
- Mutual exclusivity of roles is completely suspended during Emergency mode, allowing users to hold such roles temporarily.  
- Emergency privileges granted to administrators are exclusive to Emergency mode and must be revoked upon its conclusion.  
- Delegated roles assigned during Emergency mode must be revoked when Emergency mode ends. Delegated roles assigned before Emergency mode remain active unless expired or revoked.  
- Administrators must update their credentials immediately after Emergency mode ends and before resuming normal system operation.
